\f1\fs22 Eloise sat down with them in luxurious dining chairs around a circular, ornate polished timber table, in an impeccably appointed spacious room with a panoramic view over the ridge to the north-east.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Have you any idea,\'92 she started, \'91how I\'92ve had to negotiate to stop Fridge Force from barging onto my property, demanding to investigate an infraction of the 
\f2\i Refrigeration Secrets Act
\f1\i0 ? Luckily, I persuaded them to accept the piece of equipment you lifted from the fridge so they can verify you didn\'92t open it. Who knows how long that will keep them at bay.\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>The three hid their ruddily embarrassed faces by looking into their laps.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Please tell me you didn\'92t open it,\'92 Eloise asked in a voice so quiet, it was the most threatening thing any of the three had ever heard.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Hayley choked and swallowed. \'91No. I didn\'92t open it.\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91I mean, you\'92re a police officer.\'92 Eloise actually sounded flabbergasted. \'91And a smart, honest one at that. Surely you\'92d be acquainted with the 
\f2\i Refrigeration Secrets Act
\f1\i0 .\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91I am\'92. Hayley was intimately acquainted with said Act; every competent police officer\'97which included Hayley and no one else she knew\'97needed to know how to tiptoe around the draconian legislation which could apprehend anyone, any time, for any excuse.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Eloise threw her hands up. \'91Heaven knows, I can handle the government, the police and even PAPER, but Fridge Force? You know they can disable any stasis or cooling unit, anywhere, any time, for any reason? Sure, I could probably blast their whole religious order back to the dreamtime, but\'97and let me make this knife-edge clear\'97
\f2\i I might never drink chilled champagne again
